 `/ui/` shows the lead book in a browser: a summary that adds up, the leads, and the items that need a person. The pages read the lead book through a second, read-only database connection (a write through it fails, and one test shows that); the buttons that retry or resolve an item call the same `/review` routes as everything else. Every request, including the pages, must come with a `Host` header that names this computer (or a name from `DESK_ALLOWED_HOSTS`), and a request from a page on another address (a different `Origin`, or `Sec-Fetch-Site` other than `same-origin`) is refused with 403 before anything is read. The exact routes are in `contract.md`.
 
